'' THE RECEIVER IS THE FIRST ARGUMENT of an instance method. fbc declares
'' 'void _ZN1T1MEi( struct $1T*, int32 )'; tiko-lang emitted 'call void _ZN1T1MEi(%5)' -- the
'' right mangled name, the wrong arguments, and no decline, so it counted as fully
'' lowered. A mangled name that says member and a call that does not pass one is the
'' worst shape this kind of bug can have.
''
'' 'obj.M' passes the receiver's ADDRESS; 'p->M' passes the pointer, which is already one.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/receiver.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN1T1MEi(@obj,
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 _ZN1T1GEv(@obj)
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
